# Redstrike tool roster — single source of truth for scripts/doctor.sh + scripts/install.sh
#
# One tool per line, 5 pipe-separated fields:
#   command | category | method | spec | note
#
#   command  the binary doctor.sh checks with `command -v`. Comma-separated = alternatives
#            (present if ANY resolves). A leading @ means "path exists" instead (e.g. @/usr/share/seclists).
#   category recon web password binary fuzzing ad cloud container mobile iot wireless
#            llm aimodel crypto sca intercept glue wordlists
#   method   apt pipx pip go gem npm cargo pdtm script git manual
#   spec     the package / module path / url / tool-name the method consumes
#   note     short free-text (NO pipe char); shown by doctor for manual items
#
# Platform: Kali / Debian / Parrot (Linux). `apt` assumes a Kali-like repo; on plain Debian/Parrot
# some apt names are missing — run doctor.sh to see the gaps and install those by their listed method.
# `manual` tools are GUI apps, Windows/.NET agents staged onto targets, or hardware/vendor installers
# that can't be apt-dropped on the tester host; INSTALL.md documents each.

# == glue (always needed: orchestration, parsing, language runtimes) ==
jq|glue|apt|jq|
rg|glue|apt|ripgrep|ripgrep binary is `rg`
yq|glue|apt|yq|
curl|glue|apt|curl|
git|glue|apt|git|
python3|glue|apt|python3|
pip3,pip|glue|apt|python3-pip|
pipx|glue|apt|pipx|run `pipx ensurepath` after install
go|glue|apt|golang-go|needed for pdtm/go tools; Kali ships a current Go
cargo|glue|apt|cargo|Rust toolchain, for cargo tools
gem|glue|apt|ruby|Ruby, for gem tools
npm,node|glue|apt|npm|Node + npm, for npm tools

